ts effective alias — not only on ticket creation.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Fix: 'Any event file appended to a ticket dir bumps that dir's mtime ... so the fingerprint changes whenever any input to an effective alias could have changed'","AC4: '... cache invalidation on ticket creation, each pinned by test' — names only creation, not event-append/alias-change on an existing dir"],"finding":"The fix relies on TWO fingerprint-change triggers — ticket added/removed (root entry set) AND event file appended to a ticket dir (bumps dir mtime) — but AC4 only pins 'cache invalidation on ticket creation'. The event-append invalidation path (an existing ticket gaining a new event that could change its effective alias) has no covering criterion, so a regression where mtime-based invalidation fails to fire would pass all ACs.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc80ba265576e3f6d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC4 / Fix section","norm_id":"n0ffaa23e40d8480a","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An existing ticket's alias is changed via a new event; a stale cached index resolves to the old alias but the create-only invalidation test still passes"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extend AC4: '...ambiguity detection, cache invalidation on ticket creation, AND cache invalidation when an alias-changing event is appended to an existing ticket dir (mtime bump), each pinned by test.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternativ