 cost but AC3's before/after (as a one-time recording) does not re-assert a ceiling"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Address mtime-granularity portability: state that the fingerprint also incorporates a monotonic signal robust to coarse mtime (e.g. root entry-set count + per-dir size/inode, or accept the risk explicitly for supported filesystems), and note AC4's invalidation-on-creation test's filesystem assumption.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'the fingerprint changes whenever any input to an effective alias could have changed' — this holds only under nanosecond, monotonic mtime.","Support matrix includes Windows and 'no unrestricted-local-filesystem assumption'; mtime granularity varies by filesystem.","AC4 invalidation test is measured on 'this store', not on a coarse-mtime filesystem."],"finding":"The fingerprint's correctness rests on '(name, st_mtime_ns)' and the claim that 'any event file appended to a ticket dir bumps that dir's mtime.' On a filesystem with coarse or non-nanosecond mtime granularity (e.g. Windows FAT/exFAT ~2s, or some network filesystems), a ticket created and then re-resolved within the same granularity tick can leave the dir's mtime unchanged, so the fingerprint matches a stale cached index. AC4 pins cache-invalidation-on-creation only against 'this store' (the reviewer's filesystem), not the coarse-mtime shape.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fff2d80a9310de4a5","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix section: 'a cheap fingerprint ... (name, st_mtime_ns) ... Any event file appended to a ticket dir bumps that dir's mtime'","norm_id":"n430ccc33a24286d7","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Windows platform on a FAT/exFAT volume (or a network mount with coarse mtime): a just-created ticket resolved by alias within the mtime-granularity window hits the cached index that predates it, so the new ticket's alias fails to resolve (or resolves stale) even though it exists on disk."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the cache's concurrency contract (atomic swap of the whole index / GIL-atomic dict replace, or a lock) and confirm the check-then-rebuild is safe under concurrent MCP resolutions, plus whether the per-tracker-dir map needs a bound/eviction in a long-lived process.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Memoize the resolver scan index per process, per tracker dir' — CREATE/UPDATE on fingerprint miss is defined, but concurrency ownership is not.","'no lock' stated explicitly, yet Harness matrix includes 'remote MCP' server, a multi-request/concurrent shape.","No stated bound or eviction on the per-tracker-dir cache map (RETIRE path only implicit via process exit)."],"finding":"The plan introduces per-process shared state (a memoized ResolverScanIndex keyed per tracker dir) but explicitly states 'no lock' while rebar must support the remote MCP server shape, where concurrent resolutions can race: two threads both observe a fingerprint miss (or one reads the cached index while another replaces it) — a check-then-act on the cache map with no atomicity. The lifecycle also lacks a RETIRE/eviction bound: in a long-lived process resolving against multiple tracker dirs, the tracker-dir→index map grows unbounded.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffafe5ea5563a82c8","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix section: 'The cache is process-local state only (no config key, no env var, no lock, no on-disk artifact).'","norm_id":"n54270c48636d0294","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify that each rebuild produces a fresh ResolverScanIndex object published by a single atomic dict assignment (relying on the GIL) so a concurrent reader sees either the old or new whole index, never a partial one; note the tracker-dir map is bounded by the number of distinct trackers a process touches and document that as acceptable (or add simple size cap).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","